meta:
  origin:
    # Data product / Snapshot
    title: "Creditor Reporting System: Rio markers"
    description: |-
      The Rio markers are the OECD Development Assistance Committee's (DAC) system for tracking development finance that targets the environmental objectives of the Rio Conventions. Donors screen each aid activity they report to the Creditor Reporting System (CRS) and mark whether climate change mitigation and climate change adaptation are a principal objective, a significant objective, or not targeted. The data is reported at the activity level, by donor and recipient, and covers bilateral allocable official development assistance (ODA).
    date_published: "2026"
    title_snapshot: "Creditor Reporting System: Rio markers - Climate-related aid by donor"
    description_snapshot: |-
      Climate-related bilateral allocable ODA committed by each donor. Compiled by Our World in Data from the activity-level Rio markers data (OECD.DCD.FSD:DSD_RIOMRKR@DF_RIOMARKERS), commitments basis, constant 2024 US dollars, 2007–2024. Activities marked for both mitigation and adaptation are counted once. Shares are relative to the donor's total bilateral allocable ODA in that year.

    # Citation
    producer: "OECD"
    citation_full: |-
      OECD (2026). Creditor Reporting System (CRS): Rio markers. OECD Data Explorer.

    # Files
    url_main: https://data-explorer.oecd.org/vis?df[ds]=dsDisseminateFinalDMZ&df[id]=DSD_RIOMRKR%40DF_RIOMARKERS&df[ag]=OECD.DCD.FSD
    date_accessed: 2026-09-29

